{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_3a24e41a7d22f938e9f6c03f12b614ffa949c21a9361700581b4d36491b987f4"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Both A/ and B/ implement the same ML Experiment Tracker with experiment tracking, run logging with metrics, run comparison charts, and a dashboard."},{"claim_ids":["clm_5ef416f9bdc401ddc5ba859c7f47ee6d7d7d99082298a01c4e888538486afd9c"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The repo contains README.md, scorecard.md, race.md, slides.html with embedded speaker notes, and demo directories A/ (deliberate anti-patterns) and B/ (agent-optimized)."},{"claim_ids":["clm_8d83db98e981ef410254cf054fe37dc2a4adca5f490039653990502492b38c52"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The repo holds materials for the 'Optimizing Codebases for Agents' workshop: a demo app in before/after versions, an AI-readiness scorecard, and agent race narrator notes."},{"claim_ids":["clm_94460afd88b8f4f316442c0f7d36b23b813f91c5f6773bc5b6b7344bedb4a992"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The scorecard audits a codebase 0-3 across three dimensions (rules file/agent config, file organization, test & verification) for a max score of 9, and can be run by Claude Code via a provided prompt."},{"claim_ids":["clm_a8bc5c77fb4e9d3940afea22a711164bc501cf58717718024c74492d9431a2fa"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The repository is MIT licensed."},{"claim_ids":["clm_ad1679e983fdb1a5a493e1cd8dff7ff3a2541745e9eabd6e24f884c89c477ac6"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Prerequisites include a laptop with a dev environment, an authenticated AI coding tool (Claude Code, Gemini CLI, Codex CLI, or Cursor), Python 3.10+, and a repo to audit."},{"claim_ids":["clm_b463dc02256f210d6b0606a3e50b26cf28c29b4248d99efccf6bf1b9073d89d2"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The README documents running tests with pytest from the B/ directory."},{"claim_ids":["clm_f140188f5cf95de41cb45561b91f44fb1c4064f1cbb8d5f3d14792087e00cf04"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The two demo versions differ in code organization, not functionality: Version A is a realistic mess while Version B is optimized for coding agents."},{"claim_ids":["clm_f1e6200057e23bdc213d39db615f9405cf033585b27aa6fda56f2e0ba09f1f5c"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Version A runs via 'pip install -r requirements.txt' then 'python app.py' in A/; Version B uses 'pip install -r requirements.txt' then 'python manage.py run' in B/."}],"claim_ids":["clm_3a24e41a7d22f938e9f6c03f12b614ffa949c21a9361700581b4d36491b987f4","clm_5ef416f9bdc401ddc5ba859c7f47ee6d7d7d99082298a01c4e888538486afd9c","clm_8d83db98e981ef410254cf054fe37dc2a4adca5f490039653990502492b38c52","clm_94460afd88b8f4f316442c0f7d36b23b813f91c5f6773bc5b6b7344bedb4a992","clm_a8bc5c77fb4e9d3940afea22a711164bc501cf58717718024c74492d9431a2fa","clm_ad1679e983fdb1a5a493e1cd8dff7ff3a2541745e9eabd6e24f884c89c477ac6","clm_b463dc02256f210d6b0606a3e50b26cf28c29b4248d99efccf6bf1b9073d89d2","clm_f140188f5cf95de41cb45561b91f44fb1c4064f1cbb8d5f3d14792087e00cf04","clm_f1e6200057e23bdc213d39db615f9405cf033585b27aa6fda56f2e0ba09f1f5c"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T04:23:31Z","created_by_operation":"op_92478aa472ea456e83dc4e0e159bc847","id":"pg_99edd23e24095ec4a441d63c0d27943c","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/sshh12-coding-agents-workshop-readme-md-f89984463925-d63c0d27943c.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_3370d5924d6d5c39a588dccc7c3337f9"],"title":"sshh12/coding-agents-workshop/README.md @ f89984463925","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:23:31Z","updated_by_operation":"op_92478aa472ea456e83dc4e0e159bc847"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_2eb72eefc16934145c90cddb080826eda4ac296740027a65579b04217429a2bf"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Headless scripts automate the race: race.sh launches claude -p in both dirs with stream-json output, race-reset.sh resets git state and deletes SQLite files, and race-analyze.sh parses timing, tool usage, tokens, and test results."},{"claim_ids":["clm_3b4c72cc7897c909e5d2de95ef1897a3e48a6df68ed2038bb988fce84a6930bb"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The race narrative notes Pydantic 2.9.0 is listed in Version A's requirements but never imported, and alembic and redis are installed but unconfigured."},{"claim_ids":["clm_545e98b621d6a95adbeaecf4c734894274b6252dd19073d51192a6375b91db83"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The race demo has a documented fallback if the live demo fails: play a pre-recorded side-by-side video or walk through the codebases manually."},{"claim_ids":["clm_ad3546ece26e1932c52133eee57202d707c9d4d887d9d9a320ffc5792f83c6eb"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The race demo measures agent performance by giving identical prompts to two agents on the two codebases, comparing files changed, test integrity, timing, and tool usage."}],"claim_ids":["clm_2eb72eefc16934145c90cddb080826eda4ac296740027a65579b04217429a2bf","clm_3b4c72cc7897c909e5d2de95ef1897a3e48a6df68ed2038bb988fce84a6930bb","clm_545e98b621d6a95adbeaecf4c734894274b6252dd19073d51192a6375b91db83","clm_ad3546ece26e1932c52133eee57202d707c9d4d887d9d9a320ffc5792f83c6eb"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T04:23:31Z","created_by_operation":"op_92478aa472ea456e83dc4e0e159bc847","id":"pg_bf4d5f89a2d25082bda5f3f45a63f9a1","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/sshh12-coding-agents-workshop-race-md-f89984463925-f3f45a63f9a1.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_f65d8c557cc0541390a3cca8564853e3"],"title":"sshh12/coding-agents-workshop/race.md @ f89984463925","updated_a